2. Sample graph store
   ios/RelateBooks/Resources/books.rl is built by the wishlist-to-graph
   extension from a public sample Amazon wishlist. It contains:
   - wishlist item data (titles, formats, prices, ratings, product and image
     URLs) as published on amazon.com. Amazon is a trademark of Amazon.com,
     Inc. or its affiliates; this project is not affiliated with or endorsed
     by Amazon.
   - bibliographic data from Open Library (https://openlibrary.org). The
     Internet Archive asserts no new copyright over the Open Library
     database (https://openlibrary.org/developers/licensing).
   - data from Wikidata (https://www.wikidata.org), available under CC0 1.0.
   - geocoded coordinates and place details from Nominatim, derived from
     OpenStreetMap data. © OpenStreetMap contributors, available under the
     Open Database License (ODbL) 1.0: https://www.openstreetmap.org/copyright

3. Screenshots
   ios/docs/*.png show the app running on the sample store. Cover images in
   them are served by the Open Library Covers API and belong to their
   respective rights holders; map imagery is Apple Maps.

4. Relate
   The app links the Relate embedded graph database
   (https://github.com/relatedb/relate) as a Swift package dependency. It is
